      "leadImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3d/Club%2C_St_Ignatius_Way%2C_Salford_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7866478.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled",
      "source": "Wikipedia"
    },
    "town": {
      "title": "Salford",
      "description": "City in Greater Manchester, England",
      "extract": "Salford is a city in Greater Manchester, England, on the western bank of the River Irwell which forms its boundary with Manchester city centre. Landmarks include the former town hall, Salford Cathedral, Salford Lads' Club and St Philip's Church. In 2021 it had a population of 129,794. The demonym for people from Salford is Salfordian.",
